# Building Rendering Architecture

Buildings are WORLD-SPACE objects.

The camera rotates around buildings; buildings must not rotate, mirror,
billboard, or flip to face the camera.

Every building must conceptually support distinct:

- FRONT
- BACK
- LEFT
- RIGHT
- TOP

Do not represent a building solely as a camera-facing/front-facing image.

Do not solve camera rotation by:

- mirroring sprites
- flipping textures
- rotating front-facing artwork
- billboarding
- creating duplicate facades
- rotating the building toward the camera

Building depth must come from the building's own world-space representation.

Entrances must be integrated into the building structure.

Never create a separate 3D box/object and place it in front of a building
to simulate a recessed entrance.

Before implementing visual artwork for a new building, verify the underlying
world-space geometry using a temporary debug representation where each
building face is visually distinguishable.

Do not proceed to art/polish if the debug building fails the following test:

FRONT → RIGHT → BACK → LEFT

when the camera is rotated around the stationary building.

When modifying the building system, preserve existing gameplay,
collision, interaction, and camera behavior unless explicitly requested.
